Local Audio Zones

Based on Music Assistant Local Audio and its native Sendspin player update:
https://github.com/music-assistant/local-audio-addon
https://github.com/music-assistant/local-audio-addon/pull/34

The packaging and startup code have been modified for independent zones,
validated channel routing, device recovery and separate player supervision.
The original Apache-2.0 license is retained in LICENSE.

The image builds sendspin-cpp-cli v0.3.0, commit
bc0551c6f0c29ee1a773c4ea730bb20b71992a8a, and sendspin-cpp v0.8.0, commit
9331ace6428979982c934384702d289958ca125e.
Copyright 2026 sendspin-cpp-cli Contributors.
Copyright 2026 Kevin Ahrendt (sendspin-cpp).
Both projects use the Apache License, Version 2.0. Local patches pin named
PulseAudio outputs and retain recovery through long device disconnections.
https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-cpp-cli
https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-cpp

The player includes ArduinoJson v7.4.1 (MIT), IXWebSocket v11.4.5 (BSD-3-Clause
with separately licensed embedded code), micro-flac v0.1.1, micro-opus v0.3.5
and micro-ogg-demuxer v1.2.0 (Apache-2.0), and Opus v1.6.1 (BSD licenses and
upstream patent-license references). Their license texts, source notices and
verified commits are retained in licenses/.

The icon adapts HASSConnect artwork, Copyright (c) 2026 alphasixtyfive.
Its MIT license is retained in HASSCONNECT-LICENSE.
